  "narrative": "All twelve newly delivered estimates are already signed to their registered claim directions, so positive values support the claimed raw contrast and values below the 0.15-unit threshold do not meet the scientific-magnitude criterion. The feature_063 conditional contrasts are largely supportive of the accepted overall feature_063 association. H93 restricts analysis to participants in whom feature_010, feature_002, and feature_037 are all absent; feature_063 presence is associated with a signed difference of +0.252 (95% interval +0.169 to +0.335), so the claim that feature_063 presence lowers outcome_001 remains well above threshold even when the three large accepted labels are absent. I accept H93 but keep the investigation active because I am requesting independent validation of this key conditional claim. H100, H101, and H102 similarly show feature_063 associations of +0.259, +0.250, and +0.247 when feature_010, feature_002, or feature_037 is absent, respectively; all lower bounds exceed 0.15, so I accept and close them. These overlapping strata should not be treated as fully independent confirmations, but their consistency argues that the feature_063 association is not simply carried by one accepted label. H95, within feature_002-present participants, is also threshold-supported at +0.365 (+0.180 to +0.550) and is accepted. By contrast, H94 within feature_010-present participants and H96 within feature_037-present participants are directionally supportive but imprecise: +0.160 (interval -0.023 to +0.344) and +0.157 (-0.030 to +0.344), with exposed cells only 54 and 58. These do not establish a threshold-supported conditional effect and do not justify claiming that the feature_063 association disappears in those strata; I leave them unresolved and defer them. The reverse-direction feature_063 independence checks are also supportive of the accepted trio: H97, H98, and H99 show feature_010, feature_002, and feature_037 associations of +0.816, +0.837, and +0.814 among feature_063-absent participants, respectively, with lower bounds far above threshold. I accept and close these as descriptive evidence that the large label associations are not artifacts of overlap with feature_063. Finally, H103 and H104 decompose feature_002 in approximate lower and upper halves of feature_040: +0.747 (+0.652 to +0.842) and +0.871 (+0.781 to +0.962). Both are robust and far above threshold, so the reverse feature_040 interaction H89 is not meaningful. H89 has signed estimate +0.127 with interval -0.003 to +0.258; the point estimate is below threshold, and the direct stratum estimates show feature_002 remains strongly associated in both halves. I therefore reject and close H89, using R60 plus the direct stratum evidence R75 and R76. I request validation for H93 rather than for the borderline small-cell H94/H96 or for H89, because H93 is the key conditional-independence estimate: feature_063 presence versus absence when all three large accepted labels are absent. Independent replication there would strengthen the evidence against an overlap-driven feature_063 signal and would allow calibration of its magnitude under the conservative validation interval. These conclusions are descriptive associations within this supplied dataset only. The conditional mean differences are not multivariable-adjusted, and the large number of registered subgroup and interaction contrasts raises multiplicity concerns; however, the accepted large effects are far above threshold, while borderline conditional effects are not accepted. Causality, biological mechanism, and external generalizability remain unestablished.",
  "research_notes": "Key current conclusions: accepted dataset-specific associations are feature_010 presence higher outcome_001, feature_002 presence higher outcome_001, feature_037 presence lower outcome_001, and feature_063 presence lower outcome_001. The accepted labels are not explained by simple co-occurrence: each remains strong when any other accepted label is absent or present, and feature_063 remains strong when accepted labels are absent. Feature_063 conditional within feature_010-present or feature_037-present is near threshold but imprecise due small exposed cells (H94/H96 unresolved and deferred), not evidence for disappearance. H93 is accepted pending independent validation; if validation weakens threshold support, keep qualitative direction but reduce certainty about threshold magnitude. H89 is rejected/closed because direct feature_002 stratum estimates in both feature_040 halves are large (about 0.75 and 0.87), while the reverse interaction point estimate is only 0.127 and below threshold. All accepted findings remain descriptive associations within the supplied dataset, not causal effects or generalizable claims. Future priorities: assess H105 age-stratified feature_063; possibly H90-H92 only if resources remain; lower-priority broad screens include numeric/categorical features and research-signature interactions, but focus should remain on refining already supported associations and resolving borderline interactions only when they have reasonable power.",
  "validate": "H93"
}

